    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4814" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">băcillum</span></b> , i,
		n. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">băcillus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig.
			20, 13, 1</span></i>) dim.
		baculus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small staff</i>, <i>a wand</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Fin. 2, 11, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Div.
				1, 17, 30</span></i> dub.; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 50, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 3, 28</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Esp., <i>the wand</i> or <i>staff of the lictor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anteibant lictores, non cum bacillis, sed cum
					fascibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Agr. 2, 34, 93</span></i>
			.</div>
